    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "kind": "assistant",
      "text": "The rounding happens in **`RateCalculator#apply`**: each line is rounded *before* the lines are summed, so a deal with many small lines drifts by a cent.\n\n```ruby\ndef apply(lines)\n  lines.sum { |l| (l.amount * l.rate).round(2) }\nend\n```\n\nRounding once, at the end and to the currency's precision, fixes it:\n\n```ruby\ndef apply(lines)\n  lines.sum { |l| l.amount * l.rate }.round(currency.precision)\nend\n```\n\nThat also covers currencies with 0 or 3 decimals (JPY, KWD), which `round(2)` gets wrong today.",
      "ts": "2026-10-16T10:01:02Z",
      "final": false
    },
